---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/liquidation-risk/`;
const description =
  "How liquidation works on Aster: maintenance margin, mark price, the staged IOC close, the insurance fund, ADL and why the liquidation price keeps moving.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "Liquidation mechanics",
  alternativeHeadline: "Liquidation mechanics on Aster",
  name: "Liquidation mechanics on Aster",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Risk",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Liquidation" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Margin (finance)" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Liquidations", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/fees-and-specs/liquidations-1` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "1001x liquidation", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/1001x/fees-and-slippage` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Liquidation risk", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster Liquidation Mechanics — Margin, Mark Price and ADL | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Liquidation risk" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-rose-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Risk</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Liquidation mechanics
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Liquidation is not a single event. Aster cancels orders, attempts a partial IOC close, rechecks margin, and only
      then hands the remainder to the insurance fund. Understanding the sequence explains why some positions are closed
      gradually and others disappear at once.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/fees-and-specs/liquidations-1`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">official liquidation docs</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="trigger-heading">
    <h2 id="trigger-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">When liquidation triggers</h2>
    <div class="bg-brand-950/60 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5">
      <code class="block text-xs text-sky-200 leading-relaxed">
        margin = initial collateral + realised PnL + unrealised PnL
      </code>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 mt-2">Liquidation is triggered when margin falls below the maintenance requirement.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Aster recommends keeping the margin ratio below 80%. At 100% the position is at the liquidation threshold. The
      mark price, not the last traded price, decides the trigger; that reduces manipulation but can diverge from the
      price on your chart.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
    <h2 id="process-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The five-step process</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed list-decimal pl-5">
      <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Cancel open orders</strong> to stop new exposure entering the liquidation flow.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Attempt an IOC close</strong> for as much size as the market allows; the unfilled portion is cancelled.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Recheck margin</strong> after realised losses and the liquidation fee. If the requirement is met, the remaining position stays open.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Insurance fund takeover</strong> of any bankrupt remainder at the bankruptcy price.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-200">ADL</strong> if the fund cannot cover the shortfall: profitable opposing positions are reduced.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6" aria-labelledby="margin-heading">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="margin-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Cross vs isolated</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        Cross margin is the default: all collateral and unrealised PnL support every position. It lowers the chance of a
        single-position liquidation but puts the whole account in one risk pool. Isolated margin ring-fences a position;
        its liquidation price depends only on the margin assigned to it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Why the price keeps moving</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Funding payments change equity.</li>
        <li>Collateral value fluctuates.</li>
        <li>Opening or closing other positions changes cross margin.</li>
        <li>Realised losses and fees reduce the buffer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="negative-heading">
    <h2 id="negative-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Negative balances</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      If a liquidation leaves a negative USDT balance, automatic settlement is considered only when all of the following
      apply: the balance is in a USDT perpetual account, there are no open positions, the deficit is no more than 5,000
      USDT, and no funds were transferred in after the liquidation to offset it. Outside those conditions, the deficit
      remains your obligation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-rose-500/5 border border-rose-400/20 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-2" aria-labelledby="reduce-heading">
    <h2 id="reduce-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-sm text-rose-200 tracking-wide">Reducing the risk</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      <li>Lower leverage; the buffer grows faster than the position size falls.</li>
      <li>Add collateral before the ratio approaches 80%.</li>
      <li>Use a stop loss that executes before the liquidation engine.</li>
      <li>Monitor funding; a quiet position can still drift toward liquidation.</li>
      <li>Close or reduce before high-volatility events and thin liquidity windows.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      For the 1001x-specific distance formula and ROI caps, see <a href="/aster-dex/1001x/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">1001x</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/1001x/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">1001x</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/shield-mode/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Shield Mode</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/eligibility/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">eligibility</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
